pub fn rename(dir: &Path, old_id: &str, new_id: &str, new_title: &str) -> std::io::Result<()>
```

**Behavior:**
1. Reads the existing `.note` file keyed by `old_id`.
2. Validates the file has the expected 4-field format (id, title, pinned, body).
3. Writes a new `.note` file keyed by `new_id`, with the new id and new title, but the **same pinned flag and body** (tags are derived from body on load, so they're preserved).
4. Deletes the old file.

**Error handling:** Returns `InvalidData` if the source file doesn't parse into 4 fields. If `new_id` already exists, `write` will overwrite it (then the old file is deleted — no stale trace).

